t Analysis (PCA)? Should I get anxious about its mathematics?": "PCA reduces dimensions by transforming data into principal components (PCs). Start with correlated features: compute covariance matrix, then eigenvectors/eigenvalues of the matrix. Sort PCs by variance explained—keep top ones to simplify analysis. The math is rigorous but manageable if you trust linear algebra! My high conscientiousness would help me follow steps carefully.", "How can LLMs innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations, generate adaptive practice problems, or visualize abstract concepts (e.g., graphs of functions). For example, they could break down proofs step-by-step or simulate real-world applications. My background in chemistry/economics suggests these tools could bridge gaps for students who struggle with abstract math, making it more intuitive and engaging."
